---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Setup Guide — CircuitBot" description="Get CircuitBot running in under 10 minutes.">
  <section class="section doc-header">
    <div class="container-narrow">
      <a href="/docs" class="back-link">
        <span class="back-arrow">&lt;--</span>
        Back to Docs
      </a>
      <span class="badge badge-green">// GUIDE</span>
      <h1 class="page-title">Setup Guide</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">Get CircuitBot running in under 10 minutes. This guide walks you through installation, account setup, and connecting your first project.</p>
      <div class="reading-time">[ 10 min read ]</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="divider" />

  <article class="section doc-content">
    <div class="container-narrow">

      <!-- 1. Prerequisites -->
      <section class="doc-section" id="prerequisites">
        <h2><span class="heading-num">01</span> Prerequisites</h2>
        <p>Before installing CircuitBot, make sure you have the following:</p>
        <ul class="checklist">
          <li><strong>Python 3.11+</strong> -- CircuitBot uses Python for local tool execution. Verify with <code>python --version</code>.</li>
          <li><strong>Git</strong> -- Required for version control operations. Verify with <code>git --version</code>.</li>
          <li><strong>Discord account</strong> -- You need admin or "Manage Server" permissions on the Discord server where you want to add CircuitBot.</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="terminal mt-6">
          <div class="terminal-bar">
            <span class="terminal-dot red"></span>
            <span class="terminal-dot yellow"></span>
            <span class="terminal-dot green"></span>
            <span class="terminal-title">prerequisite_check.sh</span>
          </div>
          <div class="terminal-body">
            <div><span class="prompt">$</span> <span class="cmd">python --version</span></div>
            <div><span class="output">Python 3.12.4</span></div>
            <div class="mt-2"><span class="prompt">$</span> <span class="cmd">git --version</span></div>
            <div><span class="output">git version 2.45.1</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <hr class="divider" />

      <!-- 2. Download & Install -->
      <section class="doc-section" id="download">
        <h2><span class="heading-num">02</span> Download and Install</h2>
        <p>Download the CircuitBot desktop app from the official site:</p>

        <div class="download-links mt-6">
          <a href="/download" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">
            <span class="btn-icon">&gt;_</span>
            Download CircuitBot
          </a>
        </div>

        <p class="mt-6">Available for:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Windows</strong> -- <code>.msi</code> installer. Run the installer and follow the prompts.</li>
          <li><strong>macOS</strong> -- <code>.dmg</code> disk image. Drag CircuitBot to your Applications folder.</li>
          <li><strong>Linux</strong> -- <code>.AppImage</code> or <code>.deb</code> package. Make the AppImage executable or install the deb with your package manager.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <hr class="divider" />

      <!-- 3. First Launch -->
      <section class="doc-section" id="first-launch">
        <h2><span class="heading-num">03</span> First Launch</h2>
        <p>When you open CircuitBot for the first time, you will see the login screen. If you already have an account, enter your credentials. If not, the next section covers account creation.</p>
        <p class="mt-4">After logging in, the <strong>Setup Wizard</strong> launches automatically to walk you through the remaining configuration. The wizard handles Discord bot connection, project setup, and channel mapping.</p>
      </section>

      <hr class="divider" />

      <!-- 4. Create Your Account -->
      <section class="doc-section" id="account">
        <h2><span class="heading-num">04</span> Create Your Account</h2>
        <p>If you do not have a CircuitBot account yet:</p>
        <ol>
          <li>Go to <a href="https://circuit-bot.com">circuit-bot.com</a> and click <strong>Sign Up</strong>.</li>
          <li>Choose a plan and subscribe. Plans start at $29/month and include AI inference credits with usage-based billing beyond the included amount.</li>
          <li>After subscribing, you will receive your account credentials (email and password).</li>
          <li>Return to the desktop app and log in.</li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <hr class="divider" />

      <!-- 5. Setup Wizard -->
      <section class="doc-section" id="wizard">
        <h2><span class="heading-num">05</span> Setup Wizard</h2>
        <p>The setup wizard walks you through four steps to connect everything.</p>

        <div class="wizard-steps mt-6">

          <!-- Step 1 -->
          <div class="wizard-step">
            <div class="wizard-step-header">
              <span class="wizard-step-num">
                <span class="step-num-inner">01</span>
              </span>
              <h3>Login with Your CircuitBot Account</h3>
            </div>
            <p>Enter the email and password from your CircuitBot subscription. The app authenticates against the cloud API and stores your session token locally.</p>
          </div>

          <!-- Step 2 -->
          <div class="wizard-step">
            <div class="wizard-step-header">
              <span class="wizard-step-num">
                <span class="step-num-inner">02</span>
              </span>
              <h3>Enter Discord Bot Token</h3>
            </div>
            <p>Paste the bot token you copied from the Discord Developer Portal. If you have not created a Discord bot yet, follow the <a href="/docs/discord-bot">Discord Bot Setup guide</a> first.</p>
            <div class="callout callout-warn mt-4">
              <div class="callout-label">WARNING</div>
              <strong>Keep your token secret.</strong> Never share your bot token publicly. Anyone with the token can control your bot. If it is ever leaked, regenerate it immediately in the Developer Portal.
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Step 3 -->
          <div class="wizard-step">
            <div class="wizard-step-header">
              <span class="wizard-step-num">
                <span class="step-num-inner">03</span>
              </span>
              <h3>Add Your First Project</h3>
            </div>
            <p>Configure the project that CircuitBot will work on:</p>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Project Name</strong> -- A human-readable name (e.g., "My Game" or "Backend API").</li>
              <li><strong>Project Path</strong> -- The absolute path to the project's root directory on your machine.</li>
              <li><strong>Short Code</strong> -- A short identifier used in logs and dispatch (e.g., "GAME", "API").</li>
            </ul>
            <div class="terminal mt-4">
              <div class="terminal-bar">
                <span class="terminal-dot red"></span>
                <span class="terminal-dot yellow"></span>
                <span class="terminal-dot green"></span>
                <span class="terminal-title">setup_wizard --step=3</span>
              </div>
              <div class="terminal-body">
                <div><span class="highlight">Project Name:</span> <span class="cmd">My Awesome Game</span></div>
                <div><span class="highlight">Project Path:</span> <span class="cmd">C:/Users/dev/projects/my-game</span></div>
                <div><span class="highlight">Short Code:</span>  <span class="cmd">GAME</span></div>
                <div class="mt-2"><span class="success">[OK] Project added successfully.</span></div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Step 4 -->
          <div class="wizard-step">
            <div class="wizard-step-header">
              <span class="wizard-step-num">
                <span class="step-num-inner">04</span>
              </span>
              <h3>Map Discord Channels to Projects</h3>
            </div>
            <p>Tell CircuitBot which Discord channels correspond to which projects. When someone <code>@mentions</code> the bot in a mapped channel, the task is dispatched to the correct project.</p>
            <p class="mt-4">You can map multiple channels to the same project or have different channels route to different projects.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <hr class="divider" />

      <!-- 6. Verify It Works -->
      <section class="doc-section" id="verify">
        <h2><span class="heading-num">06</span> Verify It Works</h2>
        <p>After completing the wizard, CircuitBot connects to Discord and your bot should appear <strong>online</strong> in your server's member list.</p>

        <p class="mt-4">Test it by mentioning the bot in a mapped channel:</p>

        <div class="terminal mt-4">
          <div class="terminal-bar">
            <span class="terminal-dot red"></span>
            <span class="terminal-dot yellow"></span>
            <span class="terminal-dot green"></span>
            <span class="terminal-title">discord://dev-chat</span>
          </div>
          <div class="terminal-body">
            <div><span class="highlight">@CircuitBot</span> <span class="cmd">list the files in the project root</span></div>
            <div class="mt-2"><span class="output">[...] CircuitBot is typing...</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="mt-4">Check the CircuitBot dashboard to see the task being processed. The dashboard shows live status, logs, and token usage.</p>

        <div class="callout callout-info mt-4">
          <div class="callout-label">INFO</div>
          <strong>Tip:</strong> If the bot does not respond, check the dashboard for error messages. Common issues include an invalid bot token or missing Message Content Intent.
        </div>
      </section>

      <hr class="divider" />

      <!-- 7. Configuration -->
      <section class="doc-section" id="configuration">
        <h2><span class="heading-num">07</span> Configuration</h2>
        <p>After setup, you can fine-tune CircuitBot from the Settings panel in the desktop app.</p>

        <h3 class="mt-6">Model Selection</h3>
        <p>CircuitBot uses the Standard model by default for task dispatch and code generation. You can opt in to the Advanced model for more complex tasks -- it is more capable but uses more credits.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Standard</strong> (default) -- Fast, cost-effective, great for most tasks.</li>
          <li><strong>Advanced</strong> (opt-in) -- Higher capability for complex reasoning, architecture decisions, and large refactors.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="mt-6">Spend Caps</h3>
        <p>Set daily or monthly spend limits to control costs. When a cap is reached, CircuitBot pauses new tasks and notifies you in Discord. You can adjust or remove caps at any time.</p>

        <h3 class="mt-6">Channel Routing</h3>
        <p>You can update channel-to-project mappings at any time from Settings. Add new channels, remove old ones, or reassign channels to different projects.</p>
      </section>

      <hr class="divider" />

      <div class="doc-nav mt-8">
        <a href="/docs" class="btn">
          <span class="nav-arrow">&lt;--</span>
          Back to Docs
        </a>
        <a href="/docs/discord-bot" class="btn btn-primary">
          Next: Discord Bot Setup
          <span class="nav-arrow">--&gt;</span>
        </a>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  /* ── Header ──────────────────────────────── */
  .doc-header {
    padding-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .back-link {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
    text-decoration: none;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.5px;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--accent-green);
    opacity: 1;
  }

  .back-arrow {
    color: var(--accent-green);
  }

  .page-title {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 44px;
    font-weight: 400;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 2px;
    margin-top: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
    color: var(--accent-green);
    text-shadow:
      0 0 10px rgba(46, 204, 94, 0.4),
      0 0 40px rgba(46, 204, 94, 0.15);
  }

  .subtitle {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    max-width: 600px;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
  }

  .reading-time {
    margin-top: 16px;
    font-size: 12px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 1px;
  }

  /* ── Doc content ─────────────────────────── */
  .doc-content {
    padding-top: 40px;
  }

  .doc-section {
    margin-bottom: 24px;
  }

  .doc-section h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 24px;
    font-weight: 400;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 1.5px;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 14px;
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .heading-num {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 36px;
    height: 36px;
    border: 2px solid var(--accent-green);
    color: var(--accent-green);
    border-radius: 50%;
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 400;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    flex-shrink: 0;
    background: rgba(46, 204, 94, 0.06);
    box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(46, 204, 94, 0.15);
  }

  .doc-section h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 400;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 1px;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .doc-section p {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.7;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
  }

  .doc-section ul,
  .doc-section ol {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    margin-top: 12px;
    padding-left: 24px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
  }

  .doc-section li {
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }

  .doc-section code {
    font-family: var(--font-code);
    font-size: 13px;
    background: rgba(62, 235, 212, 0.08);
    border: 1px solid rgba(62, 235, 212, 0.15);
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    color: var(--accent-cyan);
  }

  .doc-section a {
    color: var(--accent-cyan);
  }

  /* ── Checklist ───────────────────────────── */
  .checklist {
    list-style: none;
    padding-left: 0 !important;
  }

  .checklist li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 32px;
  }

  .checklist li::before {
    content: ">";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    color: var(--accent-green);
    font-size: 16px;
    text-shadow: 0 0 6px rgba(46, 204, 94, 0.4);
  }

  /* ── Callouts ────────────────────────────── */
  .callout {
    padding: 16px 20px;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    position: relative;
  }

  .callout strong {
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .callout-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 10px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 1.5px;
    margin-bottom: 6px;
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  .callout-warn {
    background: rgba(230, 168, 50, 0.06);
    border: 1px solid rgba(230, 168, 50, 0.15);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-orange);
  }

  .callout-warn .callout-label {
    color: var(--accent-orange);
  }

  .callout-info {
    background: rgba(62, 235, 212, 0.04);
    border: 1px solid rgba(62, 235, 212, 0.12);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-cyan);
  }

  .callout-info .callout-label {
    color: var(--accent-cyan);
  }

  /* ── Wizard steps ────────────────────────── */
  .wizard-steps {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 20px;
  }

  .wizard-step {
    padding: 24px;
    background: var(--bg-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    transition: border-color 0.2s;
  }

  .wizard-step:hover {
    border-color: var(--border-light);
  }

  .wizard-step-header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 14px;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .wizard-step-num {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    min-width: 36px;
    height: 28px;
    padding: 0 10px;
    border: 1px solid var(--accent-cyan);
    border-radius: 14px;
    background: rgba(62, 235, 212, 0.06);
  }

  .step-num-inner {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--accent-cyan);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 1px;
  }

  .wizard-step h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 400;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 1px;
    margin-bottom: 0;
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .wizard-step p {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
  }

  .wizard-step ul {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 14px;
    margin-top: 8px;
    padding-left: 20px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
  }

  .wizard-step a {
    color: var(--accent-cyan);
  }

  .wizard-step code {
    font-family: var(--font-code);
    font-size: 13px;
    background: rgba(62, 235, 212, 0.08);
    border: 1px solid rgba(62, 235, 212, 0.15);
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    color: var(--accent-cyan);
  }

  /* ── Download links ──────────────────────── */
  .download-links {
    display: flex;
    gap: 12px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .btn-icon {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    margin-right: 4px;
  }

  /* ── Doc nav ─────────────────────────────── */
  .doc-nav {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 16px;
    padding-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .nav-arrow {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 13px;
  }

  /* ── Responsive ──────────────────────────── */
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .page-title {
      font-size: 32px;
      letter-spacing: 1px;
    }

    .doc-section h2 {
      font-size: 20px;
    }

    .wizard-step-header {
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: flex-start;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .doc-nav {
      flex-direction: column;
    }
  }
</style>
